278	// the bypass where a legal JSON number outside the float64 range (1e400)
279	// aborted the duplicate-field scan, so a repeated known field placed after it
280	// went unreported and the file was accepted as long as the surviving graph
281	// matched the content id. The unrelated number may be the direct value of an
282	// unknown field or nested inside an unknown object or array at any level;
283	// moving the number relative to the duplicate must not change the verdict.
